From 76cd01eaa013178b75868f8fd11b071ea9d005c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:07:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] Round 9: Update Moran laws with a stencil over a padded
 grid

A Moran target (a, b) only receives mass from (a-1, b), (a-1, b+1),
(a, b-1), its own self-replacement entries, (a, b+1), (a+1, b-1) and
(a+1, b), which is ascending source order. Keep the law on a zero-padded
(N+3) x (N+3) grid with nine per-target weight arrays filled from the
transition list, and update each row with contiguous loads and no index
arrays. Zero-weight slots add +0.0 to a non-negative sum, so every
target's additions are unchanged; the scatter-reference test now covers
11 population and update settings bit for bit. Monitored budgets charge
per-state steps row by row.

Workload: lean domain (48 Moran cases, scores on both sides), 11
samples.
Before median: 3.673 ms. After median: 2.346 ms. Speedup: 1.57x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
